      "widgets_values": [
        "For the target video, at 0.00 seconds into the target video, <Picture 1>\n(from [Shot 1]) is fully referenced.\n\nVisual Style: Photorealistic live-action cinematic photography. Fully preserve\nthe adult East Asian female architect, her natural face, black low bun, ivory\nmodern Chinese suit, hotel room, window geometry, rainy daylight, and bridge\nposition established by Picture 1. Glass, condensation, raindrops, skin, and\nfabric remain physically realistic.\n\nTimeline:\n[0s-1.2s] Begin exactly from Picture 1. Her face, body, and framing remain stable\nas only her right hand moves forward and makes real palm contact with the glass.\nCondensation compresses slightly at the contact point, but the whole window does\nnot clear at once.\n[1.2s-3.8s] Keeping her palm against the glass, she wipes one slow continuous arc\ntoward the upper right. Only the area physically crossed by her palm becomes\nprogressively clear, with tiny wet droplets remaining along its edge. The stone\narch bridge and river reflection already hidden behind the fog gradually emerge\nalong the wiped path. Her fingers never pass through the glass or duplicate; her\nface and clothing do not change.\n[3.8s-5s] She stops with her palm at the end of the arc and shifts her gaze toward\nthe revealed bridge. Hold the stable result for the final half-second.\n\nCamera and Transitions: One fixed three-quarter medium-close shot with only subtle\nnatural breathing. No push-in, pan, cut, or dissolve.\n\nAudio: Fine rain continues outside with very soft interior room tone. One gentle\ncontact sound occurs when her palm reaches the wet glass, followed by continuous\nrestrained wet-glass friction synchronized to her hand speed and faint sleeve\nmovement. No dialogue and no non-diegetic music.\n\nConstraints: Create exactly one curved clear path. No additional people, duplicated\narms, extra fingers, instant clearing of the whole window, changed bridge geometry,\nfacial drift, subtitles, logos, watermarks, magical glow, or motion inconsistent\nwith a glass surface.",
